The ugly part of this story is that these Chinese citizens travelled approximately 11,470 km (7,127 miles) to orchestrate this elaborate scam, allegedly with the connivance of some Nigerians.

It reminds me of how, centuries ago, some Africans collaborated with the Oyibos in perpetrating the transatlantic slave trade. Different times, different circumstances, but the troubling element of local complicity remains.

The good news is that they were found out!

Now, rather than simply demolish or destroy the facilities, I believe the state government should think creatively about how to turn this illegal factory into a legitimate, productive enterprise that creates employment opportunities for local indigenes.

After all, why destroy what could be transformed into something beneficial to the community?

Turn a crime scene into an opportunity for economic development….now, that would be thinking outside the box!

